Open PortAudio by its soname on QNX, where find_library() finds nothing

ctypes.util.find_library() asks ldconfig, gcc or ld, none of which a QNX
target has, so sounddevice stopped with "PortAudio library not found".
The runtime loader finds libportaudio.so by its soname.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/src/sounddevice.py
+++ b/src/sounddevice.py
@@ -84,11 +84,17 @@
             _libname = 'libportaudio' + _platform_suffix + '-asio.dll'
         else:
             _libname = 'libportaudio' + _platform_suffix + '.dll'
+    elif _sys.platform.startswith('qnx'):
+        # ctypes.util.find_library() finds nothing on QNX (it asks ldconfig,
+        # gcc or ld, which a QNX target does not have): the runtime loader
+        # finds the library by its soname.
+        _libname = 'libportaudio.so'
     else:
         raise
-    import _sounddevice_data
-    _libname = _os.path.join(
-        next(iter(_sounddevice_data.__path__)), 'portaudio-binaries', _libname)
+    if not _sys.platform.startswith('qnx'):
+        import _sounddevice_data
+        _libname = _os.path.join(
+            next(iter(_sounddevice_data.__path__)), 'portaudio-binaries', _libname)
     _lib: ... = _ffi.dlopen(_libname)
 
 _sampleformats: ... = {
